{
 "produced_by": "Scratch script run through benchboard on 2026-11-10, not kept in the repository. For each case (mean, chance of exactly zero, power) it solved the dispersion phi = mean^(2-p) / (lambda (2-p)) with lambda = -ln(zero), then recorded (1) TweedieLSS().cdf(y, theta) and .quantile(p, theta) of superglm.distributional.families.tweedie with theta = [mean, phi, p] (scipy gammainc series, Poisson tail tolerance 1e-12), and (2) the same compound Poisson-gamma sums in mpmath at 40 digits: F(y) = exp(-lambda) + sum_n b_n P(n a, y / g), S(y) = sum_n b_n Q(n a, y / g) and log10 of y f(y) ln 10 = log10 sum_n b_n (y/g)^(n a) exp(-y/g) / Gamma(n a), with b_n the Poisson probabilities, a = (2-p)/(p-1), g = phi (p-1) mean^(p-1). Quantile levels are zero + t (1 - zero) for t in 1e-6 .. 0.95, then 0.999 and 0.9999; amounts are those quantiles, 1e-6 and 1e-3 times the mean, and 1.5 and 2.5 times the 1-in-10,000 amount.",
